Title: Rain on Fifth Street

EXT. CITY STREET - NIGHT

Rain hammers the empty street. Neon signs flicker. Somewhere a siren WAILS.

JACK MORGAN (40s), a tired detective in a wrinkled trench coat and a grey fedora, lights a cigarette under a broken streetlamp.

JACK (V.O.)
This city never sleeps. Neither do I.

A black car pulls up. VERONICA LANE (30s), elegant, platinum blonde hair, red evening dress, steps out.

VERONICA
You're a hard man to find, Mr. Morgan.

JACK
That's the idea.

She walks to him and hands him an envelope.

BANG! A gunshot. Jack pushes Veronica to the ground.

INT. JACK'S OFFICE - LATER

Jack sits behind his desk. Veronica paces nervously.

JACK (CONT'D)
Who wants you dead, Miss Lane?

VERONICA
(trembling)
My husband.

Jack stands up, walks to the window and looks outside.

CUT TO:
